<!--
  SYNTHETIC fixture — relabeled by re-audit finding N7.

  This file is NOT a real ioreg capture, and the previous header's claim
  that its values were transcribed from a real "macOS 27.2" machine was
  wrong and is retracted. The sandbox has no Mac, so `ioreg -r -n
  AppleSmartBattery -d 1 -a -x` could not be captured here. Nothing in
  this repository verifies real-hardware behavior; the platform
  collectors remain fixture-tested only.

  The KEY LAYOUT mirrors what real Apple-silicon macOS emits as described
  in re-audit finding N7 (observed on a MacBook Air M4, macOS 26.6.2):
  Temperature present at top level, capacity and cycle data via
  NominalChargeCapacity / DesignCapacity / DesignCycleCount9C (there is
  no CycleLimit key on that machine), NO top-level FullChargeCapacity,
  and a BatteryData child dict carrying nested copies of the firmware
  values. The parser must read from either level.

  The numeric values are synthetic and kept from the earlier fixture
  version; only their plausibility, not their provenance, is claimed.
-->
